5. CI -- pre-existing gap, named not papered over
================================================================================

QA's first blocking finding was that .github/workflows/horizon-deploy.yml
runs no tests, so nothing above is produced by a GitHub check runner. That
is accurate and unchanged by this item: the workflow still only simulates a
deploy. Test enforcement in this repo happens in farm/checks.py, which runs
pytest + `npm test` in the workspace before any commit or push -- that is a
real gate, but it reports only a count ("N repo check(s) passed"), which is
why this file exists.

Adding a test-running CI workflow is deliberately NOT done here: it is
unrelated to removing a fake persona, and this item's guardrails scope it to
the persona removal. It belongs in its own item.


